 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.4.1.155</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Alpha-mannoside beta-1,6-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase B</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">hGnTVb</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase IX</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KIAA2008</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GlcNAc-T Vb</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.4.1.-</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GNT-IX</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GNT-Vb</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MGAT5B</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">N-acetylglucosaminyl-transferase Vb</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Mannoside acetylglucosaminyltransferase 5B</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q3V5L5_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MGT5B_HUMAN Reviewed; 792 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Glycosyltransferase that acts on alpha-linked mannose ofN-glycans and O-mannosyl glycans. Catalyzes the transfer of N-acetylglucosamine (GlcNAc) to the beta 1-6 linkage of the mannoseresidue of GlcNAc-beta1,2-Man-alpha on both the alpha1,3- andalpha1,6-linked mannose arms in the core structure of N-glycan.Also acts on the GlcNAc-beta1,2-Man-alpha1-Ser/Thr moiety, forminga 2,6-branched structure in brain O-mannosyl glycan. Plays anactive role in modulating integrin and laminin-dependent adhesionand migration of neuronal cells via its activity in the O-mannosylglycan pathway. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941944,ECO:0000269|PubMed:14617637, ECO:0000269|PubMed:14623122,ECO:0000269|PubMed:16606368, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16857188,ECO:0000269|PubMed:19846580}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=N(4)-{beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;2)-[beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;4)]-alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;3)-[beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;2)-alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;6)]-beta-D-Man-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-GlcNAcl-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-GlcNAc}-L-asparaginyl-[protein] + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = H(+) +N(4)-{beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;2)-[beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;4)]-alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;3)-[beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;2)-[beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;6)]-alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;6)]-beta-D-Man-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-GlcNAcl-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-GlcNAc}-L-asparaginyl-[protein] + UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:16921, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14374, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:57705, ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:139507,ChEBI:CHEBI:139510; EC=2.4.1.155;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941944,ECO:0000269|PubMed:14623122, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19846580};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=3-O-[N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-(1-&gt;2)-alpha-D-mannosyl]-L-seryl-[protein] + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine =H(+) + O(3)-{N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-(1-&gt;2)-[N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-(1-&gt;6)]-alpha-D-mannosyl}-L-seryl-[protein] +UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:56252, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14438, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14440, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:57705,ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:140080, ChEBI:CHEBI:140085;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941944,ECO:0000269|PubMed:14617637, ECO:0000269|PubMed:14623122};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=3-O-[N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-(1-&gt;2)-alpha-D-mannosyl]-L-threonyl-[protein] + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = H(+) + O(3)-{N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-(1-&gt;2)-[N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-(1-&gt;6)]-alpha-D-mannosyl}-L-threonyl-[protein] + UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:56256, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14439, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14441, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:57705, ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:140083,ChEBI:CHEBI:140087; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941944,ECO:0000269|PubMed:14617637, ECO:0000269|PubMed:14623122,ECO:0000269|PubMed:19846580};COFACTOR:Name=Mn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29035;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:14623122,ECO:0000269|PubMed:19846580};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=0.56 mM for UDP-GlcNAc {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19846580};pH dependence:Optimum pH is 8.0. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19846580};PATHWAY: Protein modification; protein glycosylation.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941944, ECO:0000269|PubMed:14617637,ECO:0000269|PubMed:14623122, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19846580}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Golgi apparatus membrane{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q765H6}; Single-pass type II membraneprotein {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q765H6}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;Name=1;IsoId=Q3V5L5-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q3V5L5-2; Sequence=VSP_025731, VSP_025734;Name=3;IsoId=Q3V5L5-5; Sequence=VSP_025734;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Predominantly expressed in brain. Expressed inall area of the adult and fetal brain Also expressed at much lowerlevel in testis, spleen and thymus. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941944,ECO:0000269|PubMed:14623122}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 18 family.{ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=AAH62354.1; Type=Miscellaneous discrepancy; Note=Probable cloning artifact.; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=AAH63862.1; Type=Miscellaneous discrepancy; Note=Probable cloning artifact.; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=BAB71598.1; Type=Miscellaneous discrepancy; Note=Chimeric sequence.; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=BAD02406.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Note=Translation N-terminally extended.; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=BAE44474.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Note=Translation N-terminally shortened.; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
